course: dictionary
lesson: 4265
title: Gravely: serious or very badly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Gravely» tells you how someone does something. When you meet it, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «Badger nodded gravely at intervals as the animals told their story», and did not seem surprised or shocked at anything. Badger listens without smiling or gasping, so «gravely» means in a serious way.
explain: «Gravely» can also mean very badly, as in «gravely ill» or «gravely injured». Read the words next to it to see which meaning fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Gravely» means in a very serious way, showing that something is important or worrying.
fact: «Gravely» also means very badly: «gravely ill» and «gravely injured» describe serious illness or injury.
fact: Phrases such as «gravely concerned» and «spoke gravely» show how the word fits with serious voices and faces.
exercise: «Badger nodded gravely at intervals as the animals told their story», and did not seem surprised or shocked at anything. What does gravely show? | Silly and giggly | In a serious way | Very fast and loud | *In a serious way, showing that the story matters
exercise: The word «gravely» appears in the phrase «gravely ill». What does it mean there? | Quietly | Happily | *Very badly | Only a little bit
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «Badger nodded gravely at intervals as the animals told their story» that describes how Badger nodded. | *gravely | intervals | animals | story
test: The family listened gravely as the doctor spoke. What does gravely suggest? | Laughing at a joke | Shouting across the room | Falling asleep | *Listening in a serious, worried way
test: Which phrase means someone is very badly hurt? | gravely quiet | *gravely injured | gravely amused | gravely happy
exam: In the phrase «spoke gravely», what does gravely mean? | *In a serious way | In a rude way | In a fast, cheerful way | Very loudly
